    "abstract": "Table S1: Building height (m), density (%), building width (m), road width (m) and urban fraction (0-1) for each LCZ class.Building height (m) Density per 5m classes (%) Building width (m) Road width (m) Urban fraction (0-1) LCZ Classes WRF v4.6.0 (and later) EO Paris Data WRF v4.6.0 (and later) EO Paris Data WRF v4.6.0 (and later) EO Paris Data WRF v4.6.0 (and later) EO Paris Data WRF v4.6.0",
    "field": "Urban climate modeling",
    "problem": "Default parameters in urban climate models fail to capture the specific morphology of cities, leading to inaccurate temperature simulations. This research addresses this by integrating high-resolution, city-specific data for Paris to improve the model's performance and reduce simulation biases.",
    "method": "This study improves urban temperature simulations by parameterizing the WRF urban canopy model with high-resolution Earth Observation data for building morphology and thermal properties, replacing the model's default values with local data for the Paris region.",
    "task": "The task is to assess improvements in urban air temperature simulations for Paris by implementing locally-derived Earth Observation data into the WRF model's urban scheme, comparing its performance against default model configurations and a simpler bulk parameterization.",
